<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aniceto Lacson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1857">1857</a>–<a href="/years/1931">1931</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aniceto Lacson was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> planter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/negros">Negros</a> who, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-araneta">Juan Araneta</a>, led the rising of 5 November 1898 against the Spanish garrison on the island. He became president of the Republic of Negros, which soon sought American protection. Negros later became a province under American rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aniceto-lacson.jpg" alt="Aniceto Lacson" width="130" height="217" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original, unknown; edit Kguirnela · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aniceto_Lacson.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
